{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please","id":429006,"title":"Explain 2ed Death Rage to me please?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T11:06:21-08:00","id":429006,"title":"Explain 2ed Death Rage to me please?","content":"The text on Kuruth and Wasu-Im and Basu-Im seems a bit confusing, so lets see if I got the steps right.<br /> <br /> If an Uratha encounters a Trigger (passive, common, specific) then she's going into Wasu-Im, the Soft Rage. She suffers a modified version of Rage for her Harmony Level Chart time in minutes or seconds. While in this Rage she has to attack things/cause a ruckus in Dalu or or Urshul forms or go into Basu-Im the Hard Rage that involves being Gauru for Primal Urge Level Chart time and starts mauling all the things forever because Rage.<br /> <br /> However, while in Wasu-Im she can roll Resolve+Composure to not have to attack things/cause a ruckus for a turn per success, and only through an exceptional success on this roll can she end Wasu-Im. Failing it causes her to go into Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> She has her Harmony Level Chart time in minutes or seconds to accomplish this exceptional success or she goes into Basu-Im, or can do so if willing anytime.<br /> <br /> ....That seems rather rough to require an exceptional success and to draw out rolling for such a long period of time which is part of why I'm confused but lets continue....<br /> <br /> Presuming the time limit is up, she goes into Basu-Im, and her packmates, if around, go into as well unless they roll Resolve+Composure needing one success per character in Basu-Im and needing to re-roll every time someone falls to Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is this story true?<br /> <br /> <br /> If so, Wasu-Im seems like a very difficult ticking time-bomb to avoid exploding into Basu-Im. Or is there a way to work out the Rage that I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-05-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T11:56:06-08:00","id":429093,"title":"","content":"It's not called Death Rage for nothing. Your reading is correct as far as I can tell, and yes, it is extremely punishing, by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:25:32-08:00","id":429151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=429093#post429093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not called Death Rage for nothing. Your reading is correct as far as I can tell, and yes, it is extremely punishing, by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's fine and dandy. It is called Death Rage. It's bad news.<br /> <br /> I just don't want people staring at Resolve+Composure rolls for several minutes as time passes hoping to get an exceptional success if they encounter a trigger mid-game and want to resist it.<br /> <br /> Can't it be a Extended Action Resolve+Composure instead if you try to resist it? Why the long time for Wasu-Im at balanced Harmony if at the end of it your going to Basu-Im anyway? Why not have the time in turns not minutes since a failed roll means Basu-Im anyway? I don't see the game logic behind many of the factors to Death Rage here.<br /> <br /> My opinions are as a Storyteller it reads to me as a clunky mechanic and doesn't offer a streamlined resolution in-game. I am fine with it being difficult/dangerous to resist, I'm not fine with the rules and directions for resolving it being obtuse or unnecessary.<br /> <br /> My hope is I'm missing something here so I don't have to house rule or tinker with it much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:27:02-08:00","id":429153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please#post429006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, Wasu-Im seems like a very difficult ticking time-bomb to avoid exploding into Basu-Im. Or is there a way to work out the Rage that I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few ways to stop it at this point. There is a gift that can bring someone out of Wasu-im, and a ritual that means you get out of it completely if you manage the self-control check.<br /> <br /> I suppose one could make a Mercy-gem like Talen that brings you out of Wasu-im if you manage the roll too, but then it shatters.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:32:27-08:00","id":429158,"title":"","content":"It's definitely a ticking time bomb. But there's a few things you can get up to with some investment and preparation;<br /> <br /> One is just trying to get to a safe venting area. The Exit Strategy facet might help here, but you can also prepare your own areas - reinforced warehouses with stuff to shred, areas of wilderness you know how to get to quickly, maybe a part of the undercity where you just don't care about anything you'd encounter.<br /> <br /> There's also three tricks to pull you out of <i>Wasu-Im</i>. An Elodoth can do it once a session automatically, and anyone with the Inspiration facet Still Small Voice can do it with a roll - take a few swings at doing it with a roll if you can pass your own roll(s) to keep some control. Then if you've got the Chain Rage rite up, just passing the self-control roll twice (not even consecutively) can pull you back out.<br /> <br /> Chain Rage, though, means that at the end of the month you need to get someplace secure and go into <i>Wasu-Im</i> without its help, and there's a chance that you could be screwed if the rite's foci are stolen or broken.<br /> <br /> So Death Rage is most brutal when:<ul><li>Your pack is unprepared for it because of youth, ignorance, or lack of resources/effort.</li> <li>Your Harmony is getting too far out of balance.</li> <li>You're surrounded by a number of triggers.</li> <li>There's too much fighting going on for your pack to safely work on helping you.</li> <li>You're alone.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:35:01-08:00","id":429163,"title":"","content":"Would not the new Elodoth ability also help stop Wasu-Im completely? Also, would not this ability need for Elodoth to &quot;talk out&quot; the Raging werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:38:53-08:00","id":429164,"title":"","content":"I am pretty sure that, through the descriptive text leading up to it, the point of the soft rage is to give you time to escape the scene and get somewhere that your Rage is less destructive.<br /> <br /> Transform into a swift shape, get a few turns of lucid action and flee into the woods/from your house/into a pack's reinforced cellar/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:53:33-08:00","id":429181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=429164#post429164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pretty sure that, through the descriptive text leading up to it, the point of the soft rage is to give you time to escape the scene and get somewhere that your Rage is less destructive.<br /> <br /> Transform into a swift shape, get a few turns of lucid action and flee into the woods/from your house/into a pack's reinforced cellar/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notwithstanding that Wasu-Im formlocks you, this was my impression as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:20:55-08:00","id":429207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=429181#post429181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notwithstanding that Wasu-Im formlocks you, this was my impression as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your correct, Dalu or Urshal. A few turns though isn't much time to get anywhere if your on the hunt or, well, outside if your Auspice moon is your trigger.<br /> <br /> The whole run away and cause 'safe' destruction thing is a cool idea, and thematic to Werewolf, I just don't see you getting super far to said place if your not triggering stuff in your territory or at home. It takes 5-10 minutes to get to the nearest park sometimes, even at full run in Urshal, not 18-21 seconds.<br /> <br /> I was hoping for a mechanic that offered dice bonuses to the Resolve+Composure for taking out your rage right there in Wasu-Im, you smash that window or your mothers favourite chair for a +2 to hit that required exceptional success or an extended action Resolve+Composure roll that made use of more balanced Harmony Uratha because they have time to come down from it, each roll is one minute of concentrated mental calm down time.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I can suggest that for the errata, but I think I might make use of these ideas in my Chronicle at the very least.<br /> <br /> The Rites and powers do help, but I saw them as useful things, not required things for a pack.<br /> <br /> .................................................. .................................................. ....................................<br /> <br /> I can see Wasu-Im's use in combat and especially for balanced Harmony Werewolves, I can also see its super duper bad times and that's also fair. I want it to be a weakness for Uratha. In my above examples I would totally enforce a Basu-Im change if a roll was failed, extended or not.<br /> <br /> My reasoning here is that as it stands, there are missed opportunities to use Wasu-Im as a expression of Rage that can be brought into control with logical and pre-existing mechanics that can be roleplayed out in addition to rolling instead of constant Resolve+Composure rolls hoping to get lucky or exhausting all your Willpower trying to hit a very high mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-05-2015, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:32:29-08:00","id":429223,"title":"","content":"They're only required if you care. A rural pack, or a pack less worried about blood and mess, has much less need of them. The complication comes in when you're approaching it as a group of players who all really dislike manslaughter and/or losing control of their characters, and you have to pay something of a tax to downplay that part of the game, but you can provide some of those tools for free or discounted at the table if it's an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:52:10-08:00","id":429255,"title":"","content":"Can Still Small Voice be directed at the user - i.e. a wolf in Wasu-Im succeeding at the resolve+comp roll, then taking the turns to chant a mantra to herself, reigning it in? Still a high risk strategy - against the spirit of the power, perhaps, or another mechanic pushing an interesting scene?<br /> <br /> hclaw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:00:14-08:00","id":429322,"title":"","content":"I think it's also designed to give friends, packmates and so on the chance to flee.<br /> <br /> So if you are with some Wolf-Blooded and you get a couple of successes on your roll they can get into a car and fuck off while you wreck the house. You pretty much are going to go into full on Kuruth but it's that little window which means you don't instantly flip out and murder people, you build up to it. Which is good, IMO. Plus there is a cool Merit where if you get a single success on the roll you can spend a willpower to snap out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:18:49-08:00","id":429337,"title":"","content":"I believe it's intended to simulate scenes in werewolf fiction (and really any fiction that involves turning into a monster when enraged) when the character screams something along the lines of &quot;RUN!! GET AWAY FROM ME!!&quot; whilst visibly distressed and often partially transformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:26:03-08:00","id":429506,"title":"","content":"If you don't like how harsh Death Rage is, Controlled Burn.<br /> <br /> Two-dot merit.<br /> <br /> Makes it ultra-easy to get out of Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> However, it formlocks you to the two weakest forms while in Wasu-Im, so...<br /> <hr /><br /> On the other hand, you could totally embrace being a RAGE-MACHINE! That works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:01:55-08:00","id":429886,"title":"","content":"It's not the harshness, its how its done.<br /> <br /> I just see the Wasu-Im as being an opportunity for some excellent roleplaying and close calls rather than a very likely transition to Basu-Im crushing time murder shit Oath breaking. <br /> <br /> I understand they're some tricks to cool down, from Merits to powers and rites, that's dandy. They don't play out the Wasu-Im though, they don't express it or direct it, they just cancel it. I think there's opportunity to explore the grey area between the Rage states and give some bonuses to allow for greater chances for Werewolves to keep it under control and reward roleplaying it, not just avoiding it like the plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:53:55-08:00","id":429926,"title":"","content":"There is often used in <b>Hunter</b> benefit to various groups that change Exceptional Success requirements from 5 successes to only 3 - maybe use it as general rule? Uratha still would need 3 success in one Resolve + Composure roll, but it's much easier to get than 5. And still Controlled Run would have sense as Merit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T00:43:15-08:00","id":429934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=429926#post429926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is often used in <b>Hunter</b> benefit to various groups that change Exceptional Success requirements from 5 successes to only 3 - maybe use it as general rule? Uratha still would need 3 success in one Resolve + Composure roll, but it's much easier to get than 5. And still Controlled Run would have sense as Merit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. I even made some suggestions of my own already about Extended Actions (to reward those with balanced Harmony and the extended time they get in Wasu-Im) and bonuses to the Resolve+Composure rolls if you strike out at meaningful targets out of that sheer feeling of rage. I can and will house rule this if its unchanged when I run my chronicle.<br /> <br /> Right now, Wasu-Im reads like a variable timer before Basu-Im, one that doesn't really reward balanced Harmony outside of combat, has a chart dedicated to it along with several paragraphs and quite a bit of page space. The chart has time on it, time longer than turns unless totally unbalanced, but that time is meaningless if you fail the roll.<br /> <br /> Wasu-Im doesn't have suggested modifiers as bonuses for roleplaying ways to cool down. Triggers appear to be extremely detrimental rather than harsh truths of the Uratha condition. It's all worded in a jumbled bunch of stuff that makes you look through every part of the book to find and modify rules.<br /> <br /> The whole mechanic has really great potential, but from where I'm standing much of it seems wasted and that disappoints me.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I should take it to the errata forum or just mark it in my future chronicle cliff notes. Is the Wasu-Im Death Rage satisfying to most of you as it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:47:27-08:00","id":430106,"title":"","content":"I also agree that the new death-rage seems incredibly convoluted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:59:51-08:00","id":430132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=430106#post430106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also agree that the new death-rage seems incredibly convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems obvious to me. Trigger sends you into soft rage, after the interval you go into hard rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:09:44-08:00","id":430142,"title":"","content":"I have a few misgivings about the Controlled Burn merit. I don't like the scenario where you have a werewolf in dalu or urshul getting triggered and suddenly collapsing into a very angry human/wolf. It doesn't feel right. It's fine as-is if the character was in hishu or urhan when it triggered, but I think I'd have it either not function at all in Dalu/Urshul or at least require voluntarily shifting down (and maybe requiring a resolve/control roll itself to do that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:04:35-08:00","id":430447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=430142#post430142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few misgivings about the Controlled Burn merit. I don't like the scenario where you have a werewolf in dalu or urshul getting triggered and suddenly collapsing into a very angry human/wolf. It doesn't feel right. It's fine as-is if the character was in hishu or urhan when it triggered, but I think I'd have it either not function at all in Dalu/Urshul or at least require voluntarily shifting down (and maybe requiring a resolve/control roll itself to do that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that when a werewolf with Controlled Burn goes into Wasu-Im, they're using their two weakest forms in order to make it easier for them to control their rage. The formlock isn't a negative side effect of having easier to control rages, being in Hishu or Urhan is what makes it easier to clamp down on Kuruth in the first place.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I envision it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","name":"Taejix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:03:01-08:00","id":430478,"title":"","content":"Yeah, yeah, I get that bit. You stay low and any attempt to shift towards Gauru blows the lid off. I just don't like the concept of a rage <i>forcing</i> a werewolf to drop if they're already in Dalu or Urshul. A &quot;use it or lose it&quot; clause (ie you shift down when it hits or you deal with it like everyone else) on the merit would satisfy me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:50:14-07:00","id":435695,"title":"","content":"You guys may be overlooking something. You don't have to make the Resolve + Composure check. It's a choice between attacking things or making the check, if you REALLY need to get something else done. Additionally, since the rules are modified for the Rage, you can attack inanimate objects instead of your friends or enemies.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you've got the time, you can run off into the night, smashing stuff and get to a safe place. I'd play this out narratively if you have 10 minutes to run, allowing players to choose how carefully they go or what they're aiming for.<br /> <br /> Or, if you're desperate to get something done before you <i>Basu-im</i>, you can roll the checks. Examples being: Getting talked down. Flipping that switch. Shutting off all the trash compactors on the detention level.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can blow Willpower and hope for an exceptional if you're desperate.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Controlled Burn is only weaker if you don't get Fighting Finesse for your bite attack! Urhan for the win!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:10:28-07:00","id":435711,"title":"","content":"It's not the power loss I have a problem with. That's fine, that's a natural consequence of suppressing the rage. It's the notion of it pushing you <i>away</i> from gauru I don't like.<br /> <br /> See, I view the forms as on a sort of slope, and rage as a landslide that sends you sliding down it. .Gauru is at the bottom, dalu/urshul is a sort of ledge halfway up, and hishu/urhan are at the top. Normally a werewolf entering rage gets sucked down, clinging to the dalu/urshul form for a bit before losing their grip and landing at the base. Controlled Burn I see as providing a sort of handhold at the top, high enough that you can pull yourself out. If you're already in hishu or urhan when you get set off, it works fine. You're stuck at the top because if you let go to drop to dalu or urshul you'll overshoot and end up in gauru and kuruth proper. The problem comes when you enter rage whilst <i>already</i> in dalu/urshul. Then my neat little visualisation goes all wonky because mr werewolf finds themselves launched from halfway down the slope to the top by the landslide. Which doesn't make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:15:45-07:00","id":435884,"title":"","content":"Last I checked one couldn't use anything requiring finesse while death raging, so a raging wolf wouldn't be able to use fighting finesse. Was that changed in the new rules? I just got my copy on Sunday and haven't read it thoroughly yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:20:25-07:00","id":435989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=435884#post435884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked one couldn't use anything requiring finesse while death raging, so a raging wolf wouldn't be able to use fighting finesse. Was that changed in the new rules? I just got my copy on Sunday and haven't read it thoroughly yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no explicit mention of that, so far. I might have missed it if there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:35:49-07:00","id":436350,"title":"","content":"Yeah Death Rage is going to have to be house ruled. My own personal preference is adding a Resolve + Composure roll to resist falling into it. After that remove the Chain Rage rite from the game all together and make it the defacto rule for how to drop out of rage. With how easy it is to fall into Death Rage in 2E and impossible to resist, it's hard to believe that the Uratha have remained hidden from humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T16:53:08-07:00","id":436419,"title":"","content":"To me.. Wasu-lm is the scene where Bruce Banner's eyes turn green and he has that panic in his face that the monster is coming...<br /> <br /> Basu-lm is where his muscles rip out of his shirt and the Hulk goes on a rampage. Think of that scene on the Avengers where the Hulk rages on the S.H.I.E.L.D helicarrier and everyone else is trying to contain him without getting killed. That is Basu-lm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T16:55:55-07:00","id":436422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Inevitable</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=436350#post436350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With how easy it is to fall into Death Rage in 2E and impossible to resist, it's hard to believe that the Uratha have remained hidden from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really doesn't seem that easy. Most werewolves will know their triggers and unless they're at the extreme ends of harmony, will act accordingly. Where that fails, Lunacy takes up the slack. Where Lunacy fails, the hunt can pick up. And where that fails, Hunter the Vigil begins. And that's not even counting elodoth and the simple chain rage rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-10-2015, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:01:30-07:00","id":436429,"title":"","content":"As well as a few other gift facets, yeah, there seems to be a few tools to help the Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:06:19-07:00","id":436434,"title":"","content":"Actually does anyone know what the number of turns of lucidity required for Chain Rage is supposed to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:07:52-07:00","id":436435,"title":"","content":"Mind, you know there's going to be trouble when a veteran Blood Talon with a full set of Strength and Rage Facets goes off the deep end\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026but then again, that's the kind of prey the Talons are specifically equipped to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:12:47-07:00","id":436476,"title":"","content":"I feel that now the Garou rage form is the equivalent of the big red button. You push it only when all else has failed and as a weapon of last resort. When reading Demon I liked how they made the demon form powerful, at a potential cost of shredding your cover. I can actually see the potential for groups to avoid the war form at all costs out of fear of falling into the death rage.<br /> <br /> Quick question, when a werewolf experiences a trigger, do they automatically call into the death rage or do the get a composure roll? So it a werewolf gets wounded by silver, is that an automatic death rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:40:53-07:00","id":436559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=436476#post436476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, when a werewolf experiences a trigger, do they automatically call into the death rage or do the get a composure roll? So it a werewolf gets wounded by silver, is that an automatic death rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>They automatically get into Wasu-Im.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T05:47:51-07:00","id":436923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=436434#post436434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually does anyone know what the number of turns of lucidity required for Chain Rage is supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure I intended it to be 5. I have <i>no idea</i> how that got snipped out (note that it's actually my fault because it disappeared in the draft, before it hit the layout stage).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T07:10:25-07:00","id":437032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=436476#post436476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that now the Garou rage form is the equivalent of the big red button. You push it only when all else has failed and as a weapon of last resort. When reading Demon I liked how they made the demon form powerful, at a potential cost of shredding your cover. I can actually see the potential for groups to avoid the war form at all costs out of fear of falling into the death rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.... AVOIDED. AT. ALL. COSTS. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:36:08-07:00","id":437073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=437032#post437032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed.... AVOIDED. AT. ALL. COSTS. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or used to your advantage!<br /> <br /> This can be way knowing your territory is useful. So you can drive your prey to locations that are effectively killing boxes. <br /> <br /> Every Uratha should know of a few locations in their territory where they can cut loose and rage without bringing harm to their territory. <br /> <br /> This can be why it's a Hunt. It's not just finding the prey and pouncing on then immediately. It's driving them in order to get them where you want them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:01:53-07:00","id":438225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=437032#post437032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed.... AVOIDED. AT. ALL. COSTS. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why should it be? Of course there should be dangers involved.. but why should one of the five forms be never, ever used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:14:21-07:00","id":438699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=438225#post438225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it be? Of course there should be dangers involved.. but why should one of the five forms be never, ever used?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Well, I suppose you could use a hand grenade as home defense, Bob, but strong locks and a handy baseball bat might be a better first resort, don't you think?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:22:54-07:00","id":438711,"title":"","content":"Bob's going to need more than a baseball bat to fend off the kind of things the Uratha deal with. He'd probably need more than a hand grenade, too. The enemies of the Uratha are many and powerful, the Gauru form is powerful in turn just for that reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:53:16-07:00","id":438818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=438225#post438225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it be? Of course there should be dangers involved.. but why should one of the five forms be never, ever used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Form in Question leads one to slaughter everything and everyone around you, and continue to slaughter everyone around you as you rampage through whatever neighborhood you happen to be in at the time because you got a little angry. It is never a form to take on lightly, and never for a whim. In 500 Experience over the course of several years, I can only ever remember taking Garou Form once or twice, and I worked very very hard at maintaining strict control over Kuruth Triggers. Because, you know, one slip and you kill tens, hundreds or even more of the innocent. It is a game of Savage Horror for a reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, it has its place, but it should never be the first form you consider; in fact it should only be a form of last resort, when you have absolutely no other choice in the matter. And since you are a Werewolf, there are ALWAYS other options that are far better than taking on Garou. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, I could be biased. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:55:40-07:00","id":438820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=437073#post437073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or used to your advantage!<br /> <br /> This can be way knowing your territory is useful. So you can drive your prey to locations that are effectively killing boxes.<br /> <br /> Every Uratha should know of a few locations in their territory where they can cut loose and rage without bringing harm to their territory.<br /> <br /> This can be why it's a Hunt. It's not just finding the prey and pouncing on then immediately. It's driving them in order to get them where you want them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why, exactly, would another form not suffice for such a tactic? Urshul is tailored for such things, in fact (at least it used to be). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T13:03:25-07:00","id":438835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=438820#post438820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And why, exactly, would another form not suffice for such a tactic? Urshul is tailored for such things, in fact (at least it used to be). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ushul is for getting the prey where you want them. Gauru is for killing the prey once you've got them there. If you've planned it well (and things have gone according to plan), your rage-free turns should be more than enough to take down a weakened and cornered victim. If the prey is tougher than you thought and you do need to risk rage, at least you're in an area where you won't break anything you weren't ok with the prospect of breaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T13:09:29-07:00","id":438841,"title":"","content":"Might actually work in a Hunting Ground that is not San Francisco (Non-Urban Territory is good for this in fact). And to be fair, as I said, the Character I played did take Garou a time or two... Easier in the Shadow, of course, than in the Real World. And the Forms have changed a BIT to be sure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the point remains, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-12-2015, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:16:27-07:00","id":438889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=438841#post438841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might actually work in a Hunting Ground that is not San Francisco (Non-Urban Territory is good for this in fact). And to be fair, as I said, the Character I played did take Garou a time or two... Easier in the Shadow, of course, than in the Real World. And the Forms have changed a BIT to be sure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the point remains, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Gauru is made to be used sparingly. I think its new designation as &quot;the killing form&quot; also helps drive that fact home. In 1e it always bugged me that &quot;the war form&quot; was ill-suited for use as the form you take when you're going to war. It lasts less than a minute before triggering Death Rage - long enough for a killing blow, but not for an extended battle. The new moniker emphasizes the true purpose of the form. You use it to end a hunt, not to wage war. If you need it for more than those few turns, either something has gone horribly wrong, or you're not using the form as Luna intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:49:05-07:00","id":440675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=438820#post438820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And why, exactly, would another form not suffice for such a tactic? Urshul is tailored for such things, in fact (at least it used to be). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because while you're a monster, you can be a responsible monster.<br /> <br /> Dalu and Urshul are great picks for combat focused forms where you keep your rationality about you. And of course, you have the few precious free turns available to you in Gauru.<br /> <br /> ...But you're not perfect.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be IN Gauru to be triggered into Death Rage. You can lose control.<br /> <br /> If you're intending on placing yourself into a stressful situation where your control may be tested (say for instance, combat), then why not be the responsible monster you should be and select your battleground carefully so that when you do go into Death Rage, you don't damage things you care about?<br /> <br /> In such a place, you and your packmates can cut loose. To stop resisting that call of the Hard Rage and just give into it. After all, you've prepared your territory in advance and whatever you're fighting... a Pack of raging werewolves will put it down hard. Why fear and avoid what you are when, with some foresight and planning, you can revel in the fundamental meaning of what you were born to do?<br /> <br /> Honor your territory. Build yourself an abattoir for the purpose of blood hitting the ground and walls. And above all else, warn the Wolf-Blooded and humans of your pack that when the howls of the Hunt fill the moonlit night, to stay away from the killing grounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:26:21-07:00","id":445000,"title":"","content":"Yes, you're not perfect, and yes, you may go into Kuruth at any time. I agree...<br /> <br /> That does not mean you tempt such lunacy by taking on a Form that is mere hairs away from going complete bonkers. And yes, you select your battlegrounds carefully lest you carry over into a location that is less than advantageous for you, but you STILL DO not tempt fate by taking on the one form that puts you so close to lunacy yourself that you may never resist its urges.<br /> <br /> The RESPONSIBLE thing to do it to learn to control your rages and to plan for those instances where you may lose control (because you ARE a monster). There is even a Fetish for such times... it is called a Mercy Gem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Loss of control to Kuruth is not something that you just allow to happen because you think it is okay. You fight it tooth and claw and keep it submerged lest you kill those around you that actually mean something to you. Losing control SHOULD BE TRAGIC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, I know, I am odd... that's okay though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:02:17-07:00","id":445037,"title":"","content":"I mean. You are fully aware of exactly how long you can spend in Gauru before Kuruth kicks in. You even get a courtesy &quot;shift into another form or enter Basu-Im next turn&quot; option. Gauru doesn't actually carry any greater risk than any other form, so long as you respect its purpose (attack *something* every turn) and it's limitations (change forms when your time runs out). To not use your most powerful form just because it has a built-in countdown to rage timer is nonsense when you are fully capable of just leaving the form when the timer runs out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:31:44-07:00","id":445068,"title":"","content":"Plus when you shift, your packmates have an opportunity to shift, and death raging werewolves don't usually target other death raging werewolves.<br /> <br /> There's also a rite which allows you to make the hard rage easy to avert from the soft rage.<br /> <br /> Did you read the book, Tymeaus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:37:25-07:00","id":445074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445068#post445068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus when you shift, your packmates have an opportunity to shift, and death raging werewolves don't usually target other death raging werewolves.<br /> <br /> There's also a rite which allows you to make the hard rage easy to avert from the soft rage.<br /> <br /> Did you read the book, Tymeaus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tymeaus doesn't like or use the 2e rules. He reads the new books for the fluff alone. I wouldn't blane him if he skimmed over the crunchy bits if they don't interest him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:51:06-07:00","id":445115,"title":"","content":"Which is a shame, because the crunch has a lot of the fluff wrapped in it. <br /> <br /> Like how a whole bunch of facets that cost essence to use activate automatically for free in basu-im. The reason werewolves don't avoid kuruth at <i>all</i> costs is because when the chips are down they can kick MAJOR ASS on an empty fuel tank. The raw, primal fury of the snarling death machine can be a tempting button to push. Yes, it's reckless. Werewolves are not really known for their high quantities of reck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T18:15:32-07:00","id":445145,"title":"","content":"Plus it's not as likely to hurt packmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:28:06-07:00","id":445534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445000#post445000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you're not perfect, and yes, you may go into Kuruth at any time. I agree...<br /> <br /> That does not mean you tempt such lunacy by taking on a Form that is mere hairs away from going complete bonkers. And yes, you select your battlegrounds carefully lest you carry over into a location that is less than advantageous for you, but you STILL DO not tempt fate by taking on the one form that puts you so close to lunacy yourself that you may never resist its urges.<br /> <br /> The RESPONSIBLE thing to do it to learn to control your rages and to plan for those instances where you may lose control (because you ARE a monster). There is even a Fetish for such times... it is called a Mercy Gem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Loss of control to Kuruth is not something that you just allow to happen because you think it is okay. You fight it tooth and claw and keep it submerged lest you kill those around you that actually mean something to you. Losing control SHOULD BE TRAGIC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, I know, I am odd... that's okay though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds repressive, to be honest.<br /> <br /> The Death Rage isn't something you can keep bottled up forever and never have to deal with. If that's how it's treated, then yes. You losing control will always be tragic because you'll have never confronted your nature and learned to live with it. It's avoidance. It's repression.<br /> <br /> A werewolf that revels in the Death Rage and seeks any opportunity to go into it is a danger to everyone, certainly. But never learning how to utilize the Death Rage means you'll never learn your limits. It's just as much of a problem, only from the other direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:30:54-07:00","id":445536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445115#post445115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a shame, because the crunch has a lot of the fluff wrapped in it.<br /> <br /> Like how a whole bunch of facets that cost essence to use activate automatically for free in basu-im. The reason werewolves don't avoid kuruth at <i>all</i> costs is because when the chips are down they can kick MAJOR ASS on an empty fuel tank. The raw, primal fury of the snarling death machine can be a tempting button to push. Yes, it's reckless. Werewolves are not really known for their high quantities of reck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering some of the enemies the Uratha face... I very much see Kuruth as a Big Red Emergency button. You hit it when you need to win the fight and damn the consequences, because if you lose the fight then you won't need to worry about picking up the pieces afterwards. You'll be dead.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, you just gotta Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:18:58-07:00","id":445706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445536#post445536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Considering some of the enemies the Uratha face... I very much see Kuruth as a Big Red Emergency button. You hit it when you need to win the fight and damn the consequences, because if you lose the fight then you won't need to worry about picking up the pieces afterwards. You'll be dead.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, you just gotta Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... It is a form of absolute last resort... when you have absolutely no other choice. Thing is, there are ALWAYS other choices that can be pursued. But assuming that choice has been reduced to no choice, then you gotta rage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But then you gotta <i><b>live </b></i>with those consequences that you so casually tossed aside. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-17-2015, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:25:12-07:00","id":445716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445068#post445068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus when you shift, your packmates have an opportunity to shift, and death raging werewolves don't usually target other death raging werewolves.<br /> <br /> There's also a rite which allows you to make the hard rage easy to avert from the soft rage.<br /> <br /> Did you read the book, Tymeaus?</div> </div> </div> </div>So your position is to shift to Garou so your other packmates can shift/are forced into shifting into Garou, so they are protected from each other? That makes absolutely no sense. If it is bad/potentially tragic for one to lose oneself to the Garou Form, it should be absolutely tragic for your pack to do so (and that is exactly what it looks like to me what happens in 2nd Edition - One pack member enters Death Rage, the pack is shortly sure to follow). Kill the sheeple much, do you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The book has great fluff... The mechanics leave something to be desired, for me at least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As for Death Rage... apparently we have differing opinions on what it should mean. Not a problem, really, it just means we are likely not going to agree on its applications and consequences. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:36:36-07:00","id":445731,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what this &quot;tragedy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot; you keep speaking of is. Most of a werewolf's loved ones should know to get right the fuck out of dodge the moment they hit gauru, and you get a fair bit of warning before that happens for them to run. What would they even be doing there to get injured? The risk just isn't remotely as bad as you seem to think it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:51:37-07:00","id":445743,"title":"","content":"Tragedy is coming out of your rage and finding out that you are lying in the remains of 50 children at the orphanage because that is where you ended up before coming out of your rage. Tragedy is finding out that you ate 4 people because you were lost in the Rage. Tragedy is waking up in your home and finding all your loved ones strewn about the house and yard because they were just not fast enough to get out of your way. Etcetera... Death Rage should not be the culmination of having a good time. It is a ravening feast of violence and bloodshed. It is in NO WAY a Glorious (or Cunning, or Wise, or Pure, or Honorable) thing at all. It is death incarnate stalking among the Sheeple.<br /> <br /> It is EXACTLY as bad as I think it is... It is a game of Savage Horror after all, not Fuzzy Superheroes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I missed something here... You enter Garou for Combat and then get hit by a trigger, putting you in the Soft Rage, and then get hit by another Trigger (Say Aggravated Damage inflicted by Silver). You Immediately enter Hard Rage, yes? No rolls to control anymore from what I am understanding. And you no longer control your actions (Kuruth). Since you cannot resist Kuruth anymore once triggered, you have far less control than you do in 1st Edition (And even in 1st Edition, once in Kuruth, you no longer have control either). Except NOW, your pack shortly follows you into Kuruth because it is viral. So tell me how it is &quot;not as bad as I think it is&quot; now. Because maybe I did miss something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-17-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:07:29-07:00","id":445768,"title":"","content":"No, if you're in gauru any trigger you hit is auto hard rage. The thing is, there aren't actually very many of those. If you're at harmony 5 there's... silver. That's it. Silver or an edoloth sparking it deliberately. And there's not much you can do about the latter regardless of form. At lower levels avoiding your triggers isn't too hard, and if you get to the point where it is, avoiding gauru doesn't really help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:17:49-07:00","id":445788,"title":"","content":"So, the one big weakness of the Werewolf (Silver) reliably puts you in a Hard Rage from Garou (and you will ALWAYS have silver as a Trigger, yes)? No Roll, No Resistance, and then your Pack quickly follows because &quot;reasons.&quot; Seems far more of an issue than previously to me. At least in 1st Edition you can still resist the Urge to go Kuruth (though you will eventually fail). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Balance and Harmony - Yeah, big fan of being balanced.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Thanks for clarification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-17-2015, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:25:53-07:00","id":445790,"title":"","content":"Packmates within 10 yards who fail a resolve + composure roll. Just keeping your distance is enough to avoid it. And any packmate that did that can probably attempt to lead the ragefest away from populated areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:41:13-07:00","id":445814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445716#post445716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your position is to shift to Garou so your other packmates can shift/are forced into shifting into Garou, so they are protected from each other? That makes absolutely no sense. If it is bad/potentially tragic for one to lose oneself to the Garou Form, it should be absolutely tragic for your pack to do so (and that is exactly what it looks like to me what happens in 2nd Edition - One pack member enters Death Rage, the pack is shortly sure to follow). Kill the sheeple much, do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I am playing an Iron Master so sure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But there's not many people to kill in the Shadow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and even most cities don't have orphanages full of innocent children waiting to die on every block <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. If there's no targets in the immediate area they'll start wrecking up structures. Perhaps you should read further before deciding exactly how things look <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-17-2015, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:12:44-07:00","id":445898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445790#post445790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Packmates within 10 yards who fail a resolve + composure roll. Just keeping your distance is enough to avoid it. And any packmate that did that can probably attempt to lead the ragefest away from populated areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>SO packmates DO get to resist... it is not a forgone conclusion then. That is good, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there's not many people to kill in the Shadow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I have no issues of going Garou in the Shadow for that very reason, when you have that choice. You do not always have that choice, however. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As for orphanages, you can substitute any population convention you want and it still holds the same. Mall, Street Market, Office Building, Tram, Subway, etc. The fact is, taking Garou in a City is often a bad, bad choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:39:02-07:00","id":445967,"title":"","content":"Not really; take it for up to your turn limit of self-control, then leave it. Done.<br /> <br /> No problems had unless you're pretty unbalanced in Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:42:47-07:00","id":445992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445967#post445967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really; take it for up to your turn limit of self-control, then leave it. Done.<br /> <br /> No problems had unless you're pretty unbalanced in Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that from what was indicated above, while in Garou, if you hit a Trigger (Say Silver) then you are instantly in Kuruth. So, with that understanding, Garou is not a form you take lightly because even the most balanced Werewolf still triggers on Silver, yes?<br /> <br /> I agree that it can be somewhat controlled (metagame wise) but in the world, Kuruth is such a danger that I just cannot see Garou being a form taken lightly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not really trying to be obnoxious, just trying to understand the concept of &quot;just use your turns in Garou and then shift. Done.&quot; as being &quot;no big deal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-17-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:54:58-07:00","id":446006,"title":"","content":"Not really. Seriously nine times out of ten going gauru will be absolutely fine. You shift, you kill, you shift back. No problem. Silver weapons are not a common thing for people to carry. And bear in mind a lot of time werewolves operate at night. Office buildings and malls are generally somewhat empty at the time when werewolves will be willing to risk being seen in anything but hishu or dalu. And against something that requires gauru at all collateral damage is generally an acceptable risk. The people were dead either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:55:37-07:00","id":446007,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying it's no big deal, I'm intentionally attempting to counteract what I perceive as you going too far in the other direction.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for anyone else's reasons though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:04:49-07:00","id":446017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445743#post445743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tragedy is coming out of your rage and finding out that you are lying in the remains of 50 children at the orphanage because that is where you ended up before coming out of your rage. Tragedy is finding out that you ate 4 people because you were lost in the Rage. Tragedy is waking up in your home and finding all your loved ones strewn about the house and yard because they were just not fast enough to get out of your way. Etcetera... Death Rage should not be the culmination of having a good time. It is a ravening feast of violence and bloodshed. It is in NO WAY a Glorious (or Cunning, or Wise, or Pure, or Honorable) thing at all. It is death incarnate stalking among the Sheeple.<br /> <br /> It is EXACTLY as bad as I think it is... It is a game of Savage Horror after all, not Fuzzy Superheroes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe I missed something here... You enter Garou for Combat and then get hit by a trigger, putting you in the Soft Rage, and then get hit by another Trigger (Say Aggravated Damage inflicted by Silver). You Immediately enter Hard Rage, yes? No rolls to control anymore from what I am understanding. And you no longer control your actions (Kuruth). Since you cannot resist Kuruth anymore once triggered, you have far less control than you do in 1st Edition (And even in 1st Edition, once in Kuruth, you no longer have control either). Except NOW, your pack shortly follows you into Kuruth because it is viral. So tell me how it is &quot;not as bad as I think it is&quot; now. Because maybe I did miss something.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm getting from this is that you want to play with the Putting It On The Line rules from the storytelling chapter. Not literally, since you don't play 2e, but you do seem to want to tell that <i>kind</i> of story in what ever edition you play. One where you come to your senses after having raged and find that you've lost something or someone important to you, or done something horrible, almost every time.<br /> <br /> I agree with you, for me that is one of the most interesting parts of werewolf, and a big part of where the horror comes in. But the pack raging together seems to help with that, since now they can't just pin you down and wait until it's over. They either have to keep their distance and just <i>let you</i> go about destroying everything in your path, or risk going into the rage themselves if they get too close.<br /> <br /> Here's how it works, just in case you did miss anything. If you encounter a death rage trigger in any form other than Gauru, you go into soft rage, no roll to resist. In soft rage you're stuck in either Dalu or Urshul, and have to attack an active opponent every turn as if you were in Gauru. Instead of attacking, you can use your action to try to get a grip on yourself (Resolve + Composure roll). If you fail, you enter hard rage immediately, otherwise you gain a turn of not having to attack something per success rolled, and end the rage if it was an exceptional success or if you have a talisman from the Chain Rage rite.<br /> <br /> If you encounter a death rage trigger or take Gauru form while in soft rage, you enter hard rage, no roll to resist. You can remain in soft rage for an amount of time based on your Harmony, and at the end of that time if you haven't ended the rage, you go to hard rage.<br /> <br /> In Gauru form, you skip soft rage and go straight to hard rage if you encounter a trigger. If you stay in the form for more than your (Hishu) Stamina + Primal Urge turns, you automatically shift to Dalu or Urshul and enter soft rage.<br /> <br /> In hard rage, you're stuck in Gauru, everything except other packmates that are also in hard rage becomes a valid &quot;opponent&quot; for your obligatory attack each turn. Packmates within 10 yards who can see or smell you have to succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll or go straight to Hard Rage. This lasts an amount of time based on your Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> Normally you play out your death rage, but there's an option in the storytelling chapter where you can keep notecards of people and things that are important to your character, and you give one to your ST as permission to make you lose that person or thing as a result of death rage. You can also, under certain circumstances, give the ST another one of these cards and receive a small Benny. Then when you enter hard rage, you black out, and when you come to, you find that you've destroyed or lost one of the things on the cards that have been given to the ST (maybe one of your cards, maybe one of your packmates').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-17-2015, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:17:49-07:00","id":446030,"title":"","content":"So yes, I apparently DID miss a few things. Thanks for the rundown <i><b>Charlaquin</b></i>.<br /> And yes, I do prefer that Kuruth lead to really, really bad things. That is why it is a thing to be avoided at all costs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:19:12-07:00","id":446033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446007#post446007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying it's no big deal, I'm intentionally attempting to counteract what I perceive as you going too far in the other direction.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for anyone else's reasons though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <i><b>Aiden</b></i>... Your efforts ARE appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:22:47-07:00","id":446034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=445898#post445898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SO packmates DO get to resist... it is not a forgone conclusion then. That is good, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no issues of going Garou in the Shadow for that very reason, when you have that choice. You do not always have that choice, however. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As for orphanages, you can substitute any population convention you want and it still holds the same. Mall, Street Market, Office Building, Tram, Subway, etc. The fact is, taking Garou in a City is often a bad, bad choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I wouldn't recommend hunting something that is capable of forcing you to fight it in an area with many witnesses like that. <br /> <br /> See, here's a thing. Werewolves don't just find their target and then pick a fight right then and there. That's actually a suboptimal result. Werewolves will want to chase and harry their target to 1) tire them out and 2) drive them to a location better suited to the werewolves. <br /> <br /> If you're doing things right, then you've chased them to an empty office building in the middle of the night or an empty mall at night. And from there, damage to property likely isn't your concern. <br /> <br /> &quot;Don't pick fights in heavily populated areas&quot; seems easier to account for than &quot;never go into death rage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:47:39-07:00","id":446066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446030#post446030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do prefer that Kuruth lead to really, really bad things. That is why it is a thing to be avoided at all costs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think I get it now. Y'see, the reason everyone else is playing down how bad Kuruth is is because we want to actually play a fucking werewolf without dangling the sword of Damocles over our head for no goddamned reason.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:08:27-07:00","id":446110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446066#post446066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I think I get it now. Y'see, the reason everyone else is playing down how bad Kuruth is is because we want to actually play a fucking werewolf without dangling the sword of Damocles over our head for no goddamned reason.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of us. If I didn't want to risk waking up naked and covered in blood in the middle woods with my husband's dead body lying next to me wondering what the hell happened last night, I wouldn't be playing werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:25:28-07:00","id":446128,"title":"","content":"To each their own. You wouldn't let it stop you using gauru though, would you? That almost seems to be defeating the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:27:21-07:00","id":446130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446110#post446110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all of us. If I didn't want to risk waking up naked and covered in blood in the middle woods with my husband's dead body lying next to me wondering what the hell happened last night, I wouldn't be playing werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wrong with that. Thing is that the traditional werewolf story occupies a particular subsection of the game (specifically, I think, High Harmony imbalance, likely of the character being in denial of what they are). And that can be a fun story. <br /> <br /> Thats just a slim part, though. And it kinda falls apart if you start talking about groups of werewolves. <br /> <br /> Hell, even in modern werewolf fiction that involves groups of werewolves as characters in of themselves rather than just monsters, you see them work together to better control their members so incidents like you describe above don't happen. And that usually involves being a wolf in a setting where you don't have to worry about hurting people. <br /> <br /> Quite frankly, if you know you have the potential to lose self control and become a raging monster once a month (or on the drop of a hat) then it seems really weird to not start taking that into account in your life. The only reason you wouldn't that I can think of is... Denial isn't just a river in Egypt! <br /> <br /> But playing a game with a group of werewolves and having them all in self-denial seems... A really awkward stretch... <br /> <br /> So yeah, the scenario you propose exists and is semi-supported. But is not ideal for a group game and so therefore a lot of the material diverges from that point. <br /> <br /> Frankly if I was a werewolf, I'd want to live in the country, not in the city. Being in the city is just going to inherently raise the stakes because there is a lot more room for mistakes and conflict. <br /> <br /> But that's where stories are! ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:32:20-07:00","id":446138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446066#post446066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I think I get it now. Y'see, the reason everyone else is playing down how bad Kuruth is is because we want to actually play a fucking werewolf without dangling the sword of Damocles over our head for no goddamned reason.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are not actually playing a Werewolf, then, are you?<br /> There is a reason you avoid triggers. You can play a very compelling Werewolf game in that vein. We have done so for the last 600 Karma or so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:33:30-07:00","id":446139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446066#post446066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I think I get it now. Y'see, the reason everyone else is playing down how bad Kuruth is is because we want to actually play a fucking werewolf without dangling the sword of Damocles over our head for no goddamned reason.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I don't consider my posts to be &quot;playing down&quot; how bad Kurt is. Though I can see how they might. <br /> <br /> Instead, my posts are about how it can be a strength in a terrible time where you're already considering consequences. And that if you know how to leverage your strengths (giving yourself an area you know normal people won't be around in), you can mitigate your weaknesses (means there's a lot less normal people being dead by your fangs). <br /> <br /> Just because you're a monster doesn't mean you gotta be a dumb monster. Hell, the werewolves in Dog Soldiers understood this much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:36:18-07:00","id":446142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446138#post446138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you are not actually playing a Werewolf, then, are you?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm playing an <i>Uratha</i>. To deny the rage is to deny a part of yourself, and to deny the heritage that flows through your veins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-17-2015, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:44:44-07:00","id":446169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446128#post446128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To each their own. You wouldn't let it stop you using gauru though, would you? That almost seems to be defeating the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends where my character is in her development arc. But by the time she's accepted what she is enough to join a Pack and/or a tribe? No, she wouldn't let that risk stop her from using it when she needs it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:47:45-07:00","id":446170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446130#post446130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing wrong with that. Thing is that the traditional werewolf story occupies a particular subsection of the game (specifically, I think, High Harmony imbalance, likely of the character being in denial of what they are). And that can be a fun story. <br /> <br /> Thats just a slim part, though. And it kinda falls apart if you start talking about groups of werewolves. <br /> <br /> Hell, even in modern werewolf fiction that involves groups of werewolves as characters in of themselves rather than just monsters, you see them work together to better control their members so incidents like you describe above don't happen. And that usually involves being a wolf in a setting where you don't have to worry about hurting people. <br /> <br /> Quite frankly, if you know you have the potential to lose self control and become a raging monster once a month (or on the drop of a hat) then it seems really weird to not start taking that into account in your life. The only reason you wouldn't that I can think of is... Denial isn't just a river in Egypt! <br /> <br /> But playing a game with a group of werewolves and having them all in self-denial seems... A really awkward stretch... <br /> <br /> So yeah, the scenario you propose exists and is semi-supported. But is not ideal for a group game and so therefore a lot of the material diverges from that point. <br /> <br /> Frankly if I was a werewolf, I'd want to live in the country, not in the city. Being in the city is just going to inherently raise the stakes because there is a lot more room for mistakes and conflict. <br /> <br /> But that's where stories are! ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure. I just like my characters to start out in fear and denial of what they've become. Learning to accept it, and to accept the support of a pack is part of their development. I'm just more interested in playing a werewolf starting from the first change or shortly after it than playing one who has already adjusted to Uratha culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:57:43-07:00","id":446183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446170#post446170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, for sure. I just like my characters to start out in fear and denial of what they've become. Learning to accept it, and to accept the support of a pack is part of their development. I'm just more interested in playing a werewolf starting from the first change or shortly after it than playing one who has already adjusted to Uratha culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like that Forsaken gives you the tools to do this. It's a story I'd enjoy playing through as well. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:10:35-07:00","id":446208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446138#post446138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you are not actually playing a Werewolf, then, are you?<br /> There is a reason you avoid triggers. You can play a very compelling Werewolf game in that vein. We have done so for the last 600 Karma or so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ginger Snaps? Dog Soldiers? Cursed? <br /> <br /> All had werewolves that enjoyed being what they are. <br /> <br /> &quot;Person cursed to be a monster and its so awful&quot; isn't the only way to tell a werewolf story. <br /> <br /> So, yes. Playing a character that lives with being a monster or actually enjoys being a monster sits quite well with being a werewolf. There's plenty of stories out there that have werewolves like that. <br /> <br /> I didn't even start naming books with stories like that. Just three movies off the top of my head. I can do books too, I read more books than I watch movies! ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:12:09-07:00","id":446209,"title":"","content":"My $0.02 is that I came here to have fun more than anything else. I don't want to play a game where all of the fun options are hidden behind a wall of &quot;You'll definitely experience pain and hardship every time you do this. People will die and things will be lost. Woe is you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember the 10th Commandment: Being a werewolf is fucking awesome.<br /> <br /> That having been said, I certainly want the <i>fear</i> of waking up next to my husband's viscerated body in a werewolf game. The assumption is that if that happens then it's a result of my character being <i>really stupid</i>, not because I'm playing a werewolf and that's just a thing what happens to werewolves. Make losing something important a <i>possibility</i> sure, but not <i>likely</i>.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, do you guys who enjoy the <i>Putting it on the Line </i>style do something similar with other WoD games? In some lore, vampires usually killed their victims, for instance. Or more commonly, a bite from a vampire meant that you've got a new vampire on your hands, so smart predators killed the victim to avoid spawning more. In <i>Buffy</i>, becoming a vampire means going from nebbish nerd to murderous psychopath after only a couple of hours.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:13:27-07:00","id":446212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446142#post446142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm playing an <i>Uratha</i>. To deny the rage is to deny a part of yourself, and to deny the heritage that flows through your veins.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As are we... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Rage is a part of yourself, to be sure, but it is a part that can rapidly boil over into a horrific experience that one should never be willing to actively seek out. The need for such Rage should never be in the forefront, but banked against the day that you have absolutely no other choice, lest it get out of control and bring about your downfall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not trying to convince you here... Just a thought I had about the subject. Any Uratha will, over time, manage to come to grips with the Rage that is within himself, allowing her some control over it. For me, it should just never be the part of you that you embrace and let out on a whim, just because you can. That way leads madness and tragedy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-17-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:15:31-07:00","id":446215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446208#post446208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ginger Snaps? Dog Soldiers? Cursed?<br /> <br /> All had werewolves that enjoyed being what they are.<br /> <br /> &quot;Person cursed to be a monster and its so awful&quot; isn't the only way to tell a werewolf story.<br /> <br /> So, yes. Playing a character that lives with being a monster or actually enjoys being a monster sits quite well with being a werewolf. There's plenty of stories out there that have werewolves like that.<br /> <br /> I didn't even start naming books with stories like that. Just three movies off the top of my head. I can do books too, I read more books than I watch movies! ^^</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Ginger Snaps </b></i>and <i><b>Cursed </b></i>are movies that I have never heard of, never mind seen. Are they any good?<br /> You can enjoy being a Werewolf without letting your Rage control you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:21:07-07:00","id":446221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446215#post446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can enjoy being a Werewolf without letting your Rage control you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's what we're trying to do. For example, not letting it stop us using our most powerful form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:22:06-07:00","id":446224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446209#post446209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My $0.02 is that I came here to have fun more than anything else. I don't want to play a game where all of the fun options are hidden behind a wall of &quot;You'll definitely experience pain and hardship every time you do this. People will die and things will be lost. Woe is you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember the 10th Commandment: Being a werewolf is fucking awesome.<br /> <br /> That having been said, I certainly want the <i>fear</i> of waking up next to my husband's viscerated body in a werewolf game. The assumption is that if that happens then it's a result of my character being <i>really stupid</i>, not because I'm playing a werewolf and that's just a thing what happens to werewolves. Make losing something important a <i>possibility</i> sure, but not <i>likely</i>.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, do you guys who enjoy the <i>Putting it on the Line </i>style do something similar with other WoD games? In some lore, vampires usually killed their victims, for instance. Or more commonly, a bite from a vampire meant that you've got a new vampire on your hands, so smart predators killed the victim to avoid spawning more. In <i>Buffy</i>, becoming a vampire means going from nebbish nerd to murderous psychopath after only a couple of hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be sure... Werewolf is an awesome game and being a werewolf is indeed awesome (I prefer Werewolf over most of the rest of the nWOD line, save Changeling - though I have no real experience with several of the lines, as there is little to no interest in them in my group). It is also a horrifying thing to be as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmmm...<br /> My vampire games tend to be similar but different, in a lot of ways, but just as dark in their own right. The Beast is a different thing in a Vampire than it is in a Werewolf, but both have the potential to produce truly horrific things when allowed to run rampant. So, Upon reflection, yes, I tend to avoid the Beast as much as possible in Vampire as well (when playing as opposed to running), and the consequences of letting it out tend to be about as Bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:42:10-07:00","id":446335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446215#post446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>Ginger Snaps </b></i>and <i><b>Cursed </b></i>are movies that I have never heard of, never mind seen. Are they any good?<br /> You can enjoy being a Werewolf without letting your Rage control you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ginger Snaps is pretty good in my opinion. It's more along the lines of a First Change going on with a girl and a thing I enjoyed is it kinda shows the attitude change. Her senses get sharper, she gets stronger and as a girl in high school who isn't very popular, her sense of new power begins giving her new confidence. And that's fun! <br /> <br /> Then she starts losing control and into a downward spiral. And that's fun! <br /> <br /> Cursed, in my opinion, isn't as good and the werewolf I'm talking about is specifically the antagonist. I kinda liked her. It's story is having the protagonist bitten by a werewolf and the only way to cure himself is to kill the werewolf who bit him. I think.<br /> <br /> I remember that Cursed commits the biggest sin I find for a movie with a werewolf in it. They didn't put a damn tail on the hybrid shape! If you're gonna do bunches of fur, pointy ears and a frigging muzzle, then why no tail?! I'm still greatly disappointed in Van Helsing for this grevious error as well. <br /> <br /> Anyways, Rage is part of being a werewolf. It doesn't control you. That thing you become? That's you. All you. It's you deep down in your core without any filters, without thought, without morality. That's what you are. With no draping of civility or manners or even of humanity to cover it up. <br /> <br /> Have you ever just exerted yourself in a physical activity where you just lose yourself? Gone on a run and just start syncing with where your feet land, your breath flowing and your heart pumping? Ever given yourself a chance to take to a punching bag and hit it as hard as you can, as much as you can and just let it all out? <br /> <br /> I kind of imagine Kuruth is like that, just taken to eleven. <br /> <br /> You're free. There's no room for thought, only action. There's no hesitation. No worries. No fears. Its just all gone and you just get to cut loose. To take enjoyment in that Primal pleasure of taking things apart. To destroy and leave everything a mess and just REVEL in it. <br /> <br /> And that's all you. It's terrifying. It's glorious. It's awesome (in the original sense of the word).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:48:09-07:00","id":446497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446209#post446209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My $0.02 is that I came here to have fun more than anything else. I don't want to play a game where all of the fun options are hidden behind a wall of &quot;You'll definitely experience pain and hardship every time you do this. People will die and things will be lost. Woe is you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For me that's a big part of the fun of playing a werewolf, but I do understand how that's probably not for most people. Personally, I'm just glad my preferences are accounted for in the storytelling chapter. I wouldn't expect them to be the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446209#post446209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the 10th Commandment: Being a werewolf is fucking awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it definitely is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446209#post446209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That having been said, I certainly want the <i>fear</i> of waking up next to my husband's viscerated body in a werewolf game. The assumption is that if that happens then it's a result of my character being <i>really stupid</i>, not because I'm playing a werewolf and that's just a thing what happens to werewolves. Make losing something important a <i>possibility</i> sure, but not <i>likely</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a werewolf whose Harmony isn't way out of whack, I agree. If you acknowledge and respect what you are, what you're capable of, and take measures to avoid causing these problems, then I prefer that effort be rewarded. I just have more fun playing the character who tries to fight the wolf within them and ends up screwing themselves over because of it. Eventually, once she's lost enough because of her own refusal to accept what she is, she'll be willing to listen to what those other werewolves have been trying to tell her. I love 2e so much, because it allows me to start out with high humanity and work my way down, developing my character from scared new werewolf in over her head into a true hunter, through hardship and some guidance from her packmates-to-be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446209#post446209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, do you guys who enjoy the <i>Putting it on the Line </i>style do something similar with other WoD games? In some lore, vampires usually killed their victims, for instance. Or more commonly, a bite from a vampire meant that you've got a new vampire on your hands, so smart predators killed the victim to avoid spawning more. In <i>Buffy</i>, becoming a vampire means going from nebbish nerd to murderous psychopath after only a couple of hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be fine with a similar fade to black maybe on a dramatically failed Frenzy check, but in general, no. Maybe if I was playing a freshly embraced neonate though. I like to play werewolves starting from their first change and working through their acceptance of what they've become, whereas with vampires I prefer to start my character development <i>en media res</i>. Part of that for me is that I like my werewolves mortal and my vampires immortal. Part of the fun of being a vampire is being the jaded centuries-old creature of the night, whereas werewolves' fun comes from their more human element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429006-explain-2ed-death-rage-to-me-please?p=446215#post446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Ginger Snaps </b></i>and <i><b>Cursed </b></i>are movies that I have never heard of, never mind seen. Are they any good?<br /> You can enjoy being a Werewolf without letting your Rage control you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ginger Snaps is a great werewolf movie that I personally cannot enjoy because it has unfortunate implications for me. Though, nothing against those who do enjoy it - like I said, I do think it's quite a good movie. Conversely, Cursed is one of those bad movies that's just delightful to watch because it's so cheesy. It's a Wes Craven movie, so if you know the Nightmare on Elm Street series, you know kind of what you're getting into with Cursed. It's gory and fun and doesn't take itself too seriously. I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}